  schemaType="WebPage"
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12">
    <h1 class="font-display font-bold text-4xl text-dusk mb-4">About</h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-8">
      I'm Adriel Hampton — California Naturalist, Carlsbad resident, and the author of everything on this site.
    </p>

    <div class="prose prose-lg prose-neutral max-w-none prose-headings:font-display prose-headings:text-dusk prose-a:text-lagoon">

      <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
      <p>
        Carlsbad has three tidal lagoons covering over 1,000 acres, miles of coastal sage scrub, and more 
        bird species than most people realize. None of that is well documented online for people who actually 
        want to go out and experience it. CarlsbadTours.com is my attempt to fix that.
      </p>

      <h2>Credentials</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>California Naturalist, certified 2026 (Preserve Calavera cohort)</li>
        <li>Active <a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/people/adrielhampton">iNaturalist contributor</a> — observations from Lake Calavera Preserve and beyond</li>
        <li>Author of <a href="https://lakecalavera.com">LakeCalavera.com</a>, a mobile field guide to 80+ native species at Lake Calavera Preserve</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Sister site</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="https://lakecalavera.com">LakeCalavera.com</a> is a companion project — 
        a deep species reference for Lake Calavera Preserve specifically. 
        CarlsbadTours.com covers the broader Carlsbad geography and the experiential layer.
      </p>
    </div>
